(1808149, 248224, 40718, '<td valign="top">Grain was tougher to add to the color pics.  I think this one did the best.  The selection of shallow DOF, muted colors, and subject are good choices for a grainy image. 9</td>', 'Grain was tougher to add to the color pics.  I think this one did the best.  The selection of shallow DOF, muted colors, and subject are good choices for a grainy image. 9', '2005-10-24 18:17:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808154, 248356, 40718, '<td valign="top">It''s amazing what post-production can do to a picture.  What once was water now looks like lava.  I sorta wish it had even more grain as it is really only noticeable in the bottom left. 8</td>', 'It''s amazing what post-production can do to a picture.  What once was water now looks like lava.  I sorta wish it had even more grain as it is really only noticeable in the bottom left. 8', '2005-10-24 18:19:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808157, 247346, 40718, '<td valign="top">Great melancholy subject for a grainy picture.  You also weren''t chicken with the grain, and I''m saving my top scores for those.  9</td>', 'Great melancholy subject for a grainy picture.  You also weren''t chicken with the grain, and I''m saving my top scores for those.  9', '2005-10-24 18:20:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808159, 246836, 40718, '<td valign="top">Bigtime grain.  I love it.  It adds to the old or even "ghostly" quality of the picture. 9</td>', 'Bigtime grain.  I love it.  It adds to the old or even "ghostly" quality of the picture. 9', '2005-10-24 18:20:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808198, 248269, 20941, '<td valign="top">Wonderful use of light and shadow to make a beautiful and emotive image. Great work!</td>', 'Wonderful use of light and shadow to make a beautiful and emotive image. Great work!', '2005-10-24 18:34:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808209, 247981, 16790, '<td valign="top">Stunning use of grain to add impact to this shot without losing any detail.  Composition is excellent, and the contrast couldn''t be better.  Fantastic work!</td>', 'Stunning use of grain to add impact to this shot without losing any detail.  Composition is excellent, and the contrast couldn''t be better.  Fantastic work!', '2005-10-24 18:37:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808213, 247045, 37719, '<td valign="top">Where is the image grain?  The background is beyond the DoF and should look that way - out of focus.  But if there really was image grain the bird would have it too and I just don''t see any.  In fact it is pretty crisp and clear.</td>', 'Where is the image grain?  The background is beyond the DoF and should look that way - out of focus.  But if there really was image grain the bird would have it too and I just don''t see any.  In fact it is pretty crisp and clear.', '2005-10-24 18:40:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808214, 248362, 37719, '<td valign="top">Where is the image grain?  The background is beyond the DoF more than grainy as it should be since the point of focus seems to be the finge tips.  However, if there really was image grain the fingertips would have it as well and I just don''t see it.  Nice photo, but not for this challenge.</td>', 'Where is the image grain?  The background is beyond the DoF more than grainy as it should be since the point of focus seems to be the finge tips.  However, if there really was image grain the fingertips would have it as well and I just don''t see it.  Nice photo, but not for this challenge.', '2005-10-24 18:40:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808217, 246126, 37719, '<td valign="top">Where is the image grain?  Your subjects are crisp and clear.  No grain.  The background is out of focus as it should be.  If there was image grain it would be on the whole image and I just don''t see it.</td>', 'Where is the image grain?  Your subjects are crisp and clear.  No grain.  The background is out of focus as it should be.  If there was image grain it would be on the whole image and I just don''t see it.', '2005-10-24 18:41:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808221, 245296, 37719, '<td valign="top">This looks more a product of funky post processing than any real image grain.</td>', 'This looks more a product of funky post processing than any real image grain.', '2005-10-24 18:42:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808223, 247798, 38234, '<td valign="top">I love this - it''s excellent</td>', 'I love this - it''s excellent', '2005-10-24 18:43:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808225, 247521, 38234, '<td valign="top">I like the mysterious feel to this</td>', 'I like the mysterious feel to this', '2005-10-24 18:43:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808232, 248389, 37719, '<td valign="top">I like the image, however I don''t feel it meets the challenge.  Here is why - if there really was image grain in the image it would be all over the image and not selective as you have processed the image.  There is absolutely no grain on the leaves yet all around it and that that is touching it has grain.  In my opinion it would have been stronger if it was not selective.  It still would have impact.</td>', 'I like the image, however I don''t feel it meets the challenge.  Here is why - if there really was image grain in the image it would be all over the image and not selective as you have processed the image.  There is absolutely no grain on the leaves yet all around it and that that is touching it has grain.  In my opinion it would have been stronger if it was not selective.  It still would have impact.', '2005-10-24 18:46:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808234, 247266, 37719, '<td valign="top">This is a nice image and for another challenge it may be ok.  But I just don''t see image grain in this image.  Her face is absolutely clear.  Her arm appears a bit grainy, but nothing else does.</td>', 'This is a nice image and for another challenge it may be ok.  But I just don''t see image grain in this image.  Her face is absolutely clear.  Her arm appears a bit grainy, but nothing else does.', '2005-10-24 18:47:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808237, 248518, 37719, '<td valign="top">I see a lot of texture and get a real gritty feel from this image.  But I just don''t see image grain.</td>', 'I see a lot of texture and get a real gritty feel from this image.  But I just don''t see image grain.', '2005-10-24 18:48:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808242, 248466, 37719, '<td valign="top">Where is the image grain?  I just don''t see it.  It is a nice image and I think the processing makes it pop quite a bit.  But I just don''t see the image grain in the pic.</td>', 'Where is the image grain?  I just don''t see it.  It is a nice image and I think the processing makes it pop quite a bit.  But I just don''t see the image grain in the pic.', '2005-10-24 18:50:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808245, 248055, 37719, '<td valign="top">Where is the image grain?  This is a lovely photograph and very well captured.  However, I just don''t see image grain in the picture.</td>', 'Where is the image grain?  This is a lovely photograph and very well captured.  However, I just don''t see image grain in the picture.', '2005-10-24 18:51:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808253, 248382, 37719, '<td valign="top">I would think if an image has grain, it applies to the whole image, not just a small portion of it.  This is an interesting capture without a doubt and the processing has made the colors really pop out.  The clarity is very nice on the flowers.  And that is the problem.  Only the bee has any blur and even that seems wrong.  It should be motion blur on the bee not image blur.  And if that processing was applied to the whole imaeg it would meet the challenge in my opinion.</td>', 'I would think if an image has grain, it applies to the whole image, not just a small portion of it.  This is an interesting capture without a doubt and the processing has made the colors really pop out.  The clarity is very nice on the flowers.  And that is the problem.  Only the bee has any blur and even that seems wrong.  It should be motion blur on the bee not image blur.  And if that processing was applied to the whole imaeg it would meet the challenge in my opinion.', '2005-10-24 18:52:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808259, 248410, 37719, '<td valign="top">Where is the image grain?  A rough wall does not make image grain.  I ilke the photo and processed in black and white is perfect.  But the only ''grain'' I see is in the texture of the wall behind the bicycle.</td>', 'Where is the image grain?  A rough wall does not make image grain.  I ilke the photo and processed in black and white is perfect.  But the only ''grain'' I see is in the texture of the wall behind the bicycle.', '2005-10-24 18:53:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808260, 247482, 37719, '<td valign="top">Very cute child and a really great capture.  Nice colors and lighting.  But I just don''t see any image grain.  In fact the image is quite crisp looking.</td>', 'Very cute child and a really great capture.  Nice colors and lighting.  But I just don''t see any image grain.  In fact the image is quite crisp looking.', '2005-10-24 18:54:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808281, 247365, 37719, '<td valign="top">Where is the image grain?  This is a stunning, moody, very well done photograph.  I have actually added it as a favorite.  But I just don''t see any image grain.</td>', 'Where is the image grain?  This is a stunning, moody, very well done photograph.  I have actually added it as a favorite.  But I just don''t see any image grain.', '2005-10-24 18:59:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808287, 248345, 16790, '<td valign="top">I love this shot.  The grain, the background motion, the clarity of the subject, and the composition all make this interesting and moody; the atmosphere is just fantastic in this.  Excellent work.</td>', 'I love this shot.  The grain, the background motion, the clarity of the subject, and the composition all make this interesting and moody; the atmosphere is just fantastic in this.  Excellent work.', '2005-10-24 19:00:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808310, 247492, 42198, '<td valign="top">I love the lighting, the tones, the sense of movement, and the composition.... oh, and the grain! You''ve captured a great mood here. This really tells a story. One of my favs of the challenge. 10</td>', 'I love the lighting, the tones, the sense of movement, and the composition.... oh, and the grain! You''ve captured a great mood here. This really tells a story. One of my favs of the challenge. 10', '2005-10-24 19:06:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808363, 247522, 16790, '<td valign="top">There''s some great grain here, and I really like the composition - not fond of how out of focus it is, though, and I would really prefer that the selective desaturation be total desaturation.  Your contrast is great, the subject is adorable, and overall the shot is definitely appealing - nice image!  The only thing I really don''t like is the oversaturated blue.  Good luck, you''ve met the challenge well :)</td>', 'There''s some great grain here, and I really like the composition - not fond of how out of focus it is, though, and I would really prefer that the selective desaturation be total desaturation.  Your contrast is great, the subject is adorable, and overall the shot is definitely appealing - nice image!  The only thing I really don''t like is the oversaturated blue.  Good luck, you''ve met the challenge well :)', '2005-10-24 19:28:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808371, 248032, 16790, '<td valign="top">This shot has a lot of appeal with the deep DOF and the nice contrast; the grain is well done and suitable to the image.  I do, however, feel that the sepia tone is a bit heavy, and it makes it difficult to really get the details.. they''re just not standing out like they could with a slightly greener, less saturated tone.  Otherwise, this looks great - I love the light.</td>', 'This shot has a lot of appeal with the deep DOF and the nice contrast; the grain is well done and suitable to the image.  I do, however, feel that the sepia tone is a bit heavy, and it makes it difficult to really get the details.. they''re just not standing out like they could with a slightly greener, less saturated tone.  Otherwise, this looks great - I love the light.', '2005-10-24 19:32:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808372, 248083, 45000, '<td valign="top">Have you seen Donnie Darko?</td>', 'Have you seen Donnie Darko?', '2005-10-24 19:32:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808375, 245640, 16790, '<td valign="top">Beautiful - this is one of the rare occasions where I like selective desaturation.  Your toning is perfect here, too - this could easily be too heavy of a sepia tone, but for this contrasty of a photograph, it works beautifully.  The grain is perfect - you have a very moody, emotive shot here.  Well done.</td>', 'Beautiful - this is one of the rare occasions where I like selective desaturation.  Your toning is perfect here, too - this could easily be too heavy of a sepia tone, but for this contrasty of a photograph, it works beautifully.  The grain is perfect - you have a very moody, emotive shot here.  Well done.', '2005-10-24 19:33:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808376, 248228, 45000, '<td valign="top">I love this shot...looks like there is such a story behind that car.  Makes me wonder...</td>', 'I love this shot...looks like there is such a story behind that car.  Makes me wonder...', '2005-10-24 19:33:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808385, 248293, 45000, '<td valign="top">Don''t like the frame that much...</td>', 'Don''t like the frame that much...', '2005-10-24 19:38:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808388, 245931, 34041, '<td valign="top">I''m sure you''ve heard this many times already, but I wish it was bigger. It''s a great shot. Really good mood. This would have been a 7 or 8 from me, but being so tiny, I have to give it only a 6</td>', 'I''m sure you''ve heard this many times already, but I wish it was bigger. It''s a great shot. Really good mood. This would have been a 7 or 8 from me, but being so tiny, I have to give it only a 6', '2005-10-24 19:39:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808389, 248527, 42005, '<td valign="top">Magnificent.  The grain certainly adds to the title and disposition of the photograph.<br/>Nice work. Thank you for sharing. 10</td>', 'Magnificent.  The grain certainly adds to the title and disposition of the photograph.Nice work. Thank you for sharing. 10', '2005-10-24 19:39:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808390, 248035, 42005, '<td valign="top">Very lovely and certainly meets the challenge.  It is a delightful photograph. 10</td>', 'Very lovely and certainly meets the challenge.  It is a delightful photograph. 10', '2005-10-24 19:40:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808393, 246920, 42005, '<td valign="top">Absolutely wondeful.  Great focus and the tones just sing.</td>', 'Absolutely wondeful.  Great focus and the tones just sing.', '2005-10-24 19:41:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808397, 247365, 45000, '<td valign="top">By far the best picture I''ve seen so far...stunning</td>', 'By far the best picture I''ve seen so far...stunning', '2005-10-24 19:43:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808436, 248108, 43565, '<td valign="top">This is too dark for me.</td>', 'This is too dark for me.', '2005-10-24 20:09:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808438, 247331, 43565, '<td valign="top">The grain does not show up on my monitor.</td>', 'The grain does not show up on my monitor.', '2005-10-24 20:11:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808451, 247520, 43565, '<td valign="top">I think this needs to be more in focus.</td>', 'I think this needs to be more in focus.', '2005-10-24 20:19:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808455, 248462, 43565, '<td valign="top">I would like this better if his face was in focus.</td>', 'I would like this better if his face was in focus.', '2005-10-24 20:21:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808458, 248115, 43565, '<td valign="top">I think this would have been better with less noise.</td>', 'I think this would have been better with less noise.', '2005-10-24 20:24:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808462, 247494, 43565, '<td valign="top">This does not look grainy to me.</td>', 'This does not look grainy to me.', '2005-10-24 20:24:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808463, 248286, 43020, '<td valign="top">The grain really suits this shot - nice selection.  Half the battle was finding a good subject to use grain on and you did that well.</td>', 'The grain really suits this shot - nice selection.  Half the battle was finding a good subject to use grain on and you did that well.', '2005-10-24 20:24:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808468, 247845, 43020, '<td valign="top">Really captures the movement and action.  The grain gives it a nice grittiness.  Nice shot.</td>', 'Really captures the movement and action.  The grain gives it a nice grittiness.  Nice shot.', '2005-10-24 20:26:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808475, 246901, 43020, '<td valign="top">There doesn''t seem to be any grain to me - looking hard but can''t get there.  GREAT capture though, I love the shot, it is just missing the challenge reqs.</td>', 'There doesn''t seem to be any grain to me - looking hard but can''t get there.  GREAT capture though, I love the shot, it is just missing the challenge reqs.', '2005-10-24 20:27:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808482, 247482, 43565, '<td valign="top"></td>', '', '2005-10-24 20:30:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808484, 248356, 43020, '<td valign="top">Wow - that''s moody.  Nice shot!</td>', 'Wow - that''s moody.  Nice shot!', '2005-10-24 20:30:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808494, 248046, 43565, '<td valign="top">I think this would be better if it were off-center.</td>', 'I think this would be better if it were off-center.', '2005-10-24 20:33:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808504, 247506, 31606, '<td valign="top">Neat idea.  It took me a minute but I see it now.  I like it and I am sorry there is nothing I can say for improvement.</td>', 'Neat idea.  It took me a minute but I see it now.  I like it and I am sorry there is nothing I can say for improvement.', '2005-10-24 20:37:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808505, 248084, 42714, '<td valign="top">One thing I want to recommend in terms of composition...it''s how objects meet the photograph border...it can be really important in how the eye really connects with what''s being shot.  For example..the "stem" of this rose...is nice, but then there''s a little something at the bottom.  It''s not enough to really matter to the photo, but it''s prominent enough to notice.  My suggestion would either be more aware of such things during the shot, or think about it a bit more when considering how you crop a photo.  Just my two cents.  Good luck with the challenge!</td>', 'One thing I want to recommend in terms of composition...it''s how objects meet the photograph border...it can be really important in how the eye really connects with what''s being shot.  For example..the "stem" of this rose...is nice, but then there''s a little something at the bottom.  It''s not enough to really matter to the photo, but it''s prominent enough to notice.  My suggestion would either be more aware of such things during the shot, or think about it a bit more when considering how you crop a photo.  Just my two cents.  Good luck with the challenge!', '2005-10-24 20:37:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808507, 246764, 42714, '<td valign="top">One of the better photos I''ve seen in the challenge thus far.  Wedding/commitment sort of pictures always look great with grain.</td>', 'One of the better photos I''ve seen in the challenge thus far.  Wedding/commitment sort of pictures always look great with grain.', '2005-10-24 20:38:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808512, 246759, 42714, '<td valign="top">I was waiting for a grain photo with grain!  Kudos for the effort.</td>', 'I was waiting for a grain photo with grain!  Kudos for the effort.', '2005-10-24 20:39:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808513, 247888, 43565, '<td valign="top">IMO this should be more in focus.</td>', 'IMO this should be more in focus.', '2005-10-24 20:41:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808514, 246709, 42714, '<td valign="top">Rural photography always looks GREAT in grain.  Tremendous piece of Americana.  Looks a tad over-processed, but you know what, I''m pretty fond of that style myself.</td>', 'Rural photography always looks GREAT in grain.  Tremendous piece of Americana.  Looks a tad over-processed, but you know what, I''m pretty fond of that style myself.', '2005-10-24 20:41:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808519, 248417, 42714, '<td valign="top">I''m in love with this picture for it''s simplicity.  So many people try so hard to get a great shot.   Grain is great in further distinguishing various textures...metals and woods being at the top of the list.  Great angle, perfect lighting situation and wonderful proportions.  Not sure if you used a diffuse light filte ron your camera, but it sure has that effect.</td>', 'I''m in love with this picture for it''s simplicity.  So many people try so hard to get a great shot.   Grain is great in further distinguishing various textures...metals and woods being at the top of the list.  Great angle, perfect lighting situation and wonderful proportions.  Not sure if you used a diffuse light filte ron your camera, but it sure has that effect.', '2005-10-24 20:44:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808523, 248130, 37719, '<td valign="top">This photo has a few things going for it.  But as usual, there are a few things against it.  As far as the challenge goes, at a low resolution setting on a monitor this shows a lot of image grain and also a lot of detail that is lost with higher resolution monitors.  But at higher resolutions not only is the image grain lost, but the detail that is great at lower resolutions becomes too busy.  The bottom edge of the photo appears washed out for some reason.  Not sure why.  A slightly different crop, like maybe 2/3''s of the dam may have worked better.  Could use a levels adjustment as well as a slight contrast boost to bring out the detail in the image.  The rays are a boost.  Overall it is a good capture.  I think more detail in the crop and post processing would have made this a wow image.   I also like the play on words with the title.  Again, just would like to see it processed and cropped a little differently.</td>', 'This photo has a few things going for it.  But as usual, there are a few things against it.  As far as the challenge goes, at a low resolution setting on a monitor this shows a lot of image grain and also a lot of detail that is lost with higher resolution monitors.  But at higher resolutions not only is the image grain lost, but the detail that is great at lower resolutions becomes too busy.  The bottom edge of the photo appears washed out for some reason.  Not sure why.  A slightly different crop, like maybe 2/3''s of the dam may have worked better.  Could use a levels adjustment as well as a slight contrast boost to bring out the detail in the image.  The rays are a boost.  Overall it is a good capture.  I think more detail in the crop and post processing would have made this a wow image.   I also like the play on words with the title.  Again, just would like to see it processed and cropped a little differently.', '2005-10-24 20:46:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808526, 247720, 42714, '<td valign="top">Love the understatement in this photograph.  Turning the reflection upside down is a wonderful, wonderful twist.</td>', 'Love the understatement in this photograph.  Turning the reflection upside down is a wonderful, wonderful twist.', '2005-10-24 20:47:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808548, 246685, 42714, '<td valign="top">Another option is if there was a crop so that all that could be seen were the stairs....yes, this would "clip" the hair of the pedestrian, but think it would be forgivable.  I don''t necessarily it''s better or worse than this, as I think both have their pros and cons in terms of overall composition.</td>', 'Another option is if there was a crop so that all that could be seen were the stairs....yes, this would "clip" the hair of the pedestrian, but think it would be forgivable.  I don''t necessarily it''s better or worse than this, as I think both have their pros and cons in terms of overall composition.', '2005-10-24 20:54:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808566, 245496, 42714, '<td valign="top">The shadows and darks pop out even more because of the grain, it draws you in  and makes the entire composition seem more stark and barren.</td>', 'The shadows and darks pop out even more because of the grain, it draws you in  and makes the entire composition seem more stark and barren.', '2005-10-24 21:05:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808575, 248235, 26756, '<td valign="top">Excellent image.  If not for the clothing, it looks like it could be a century old.  Perfect image for grain.  Nice job!</td>', 'Excellent image.  If not for the clothing, it looks like it could be a century old.  Perfect image for grain.  Nice job!', '2005-10-24 21:11:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808579, 247483, 42714, '<td valign="top">Very charming and romantic photo, with the park and bicycles, one can easily take it for a country in Europe.  And if this is Europe, well then - even better.</td>', 'Very charming and romantic photo, with the park and bicycles, one can easily take it for a country in Europe.  And if this is Europe, well then - even better.', '2005-10-24 21:13:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808587, 246764, 43020, '<td valign="top">Nice shot - a shame the gent''s ring slipped down a little.</td>', 'Nice shot - a shame the gent''s ring slipped down a little.', '2005-10-24 21:22:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808592, 248343, 43020, '<td valign="top">Are those squares reflections off a glass case?  It''s all I seem to look at I''m afraid.</td>', 'Are those squares reflections off a glass case?  It''s all I seem to look at I''m afraid.', '2005-10-24 21:24:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808597, 248175, 43020, '<td valign="top">I can''t seem to see any grain - lovely shot though.</td>', 'I can''t seem to see any grain - lovely shot though.', '2005-10-24 21:26:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808600, 247365, 43020, '<td valign="top">The grain must be very subtle?  I can''t seem to see any, certainly not enough to add ambience to a wonderful pictures.  Nice capture, but lacks the grain.</td>', 'The grain must be very subtle?  I can''t seem to see any, certainly not enough to add ambience to a wonderful pictures.  Nice capture, but lacks the grain.', '2005-10-24 21:27:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808601, 248447, 15691, '<td valign="top">I think this picture will win this challenge, excellent portrait, love the sadness in his eyes and the duty that seems to burden him so heavily.  Congratz :)</td>', 'I think this picture will win this challenge, excellent portrait, love the sadness in his eyes and the duty that seems to burden him so heavily.  Congratz :)', '2005-10-24 21:28:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808602, 248269, 43020, '<td valign="top">great shot - it''ll be one to treasure for ages!  Could have used a little more film grain to make it stand out in the comp on that facet, but as far as composition goes - I love it!</td>', 'great shot - it''ll be one to treasure for ages!  Could have used a little more film grain to make it stand out in the comp on that facet, but as far as composition goes - I love it!', '2005-10-24 21:29:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808606, 246759, 43020, '<td valign="top">Nice double take on the challenge.  The image has a nice old feel to it and the grain really suits the composition.  Nice work.</td>', 'Nice double take on the challenge.  The image has a nice old feel to it and the grain really suits the composition.  Nice work.', '2005-10-24 21:30:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808607, 247311, 39057, '<td valign="top">Very nice......just those two lines at the lower left kill me...maybe I''m missing something?   ...7</td>', 'Very nice......just those two lines at the lower left kill me...maybe I''m missing something?   ...7', '2005-10-24 21:30:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(1808608, 248099, 43020, '<td valign="top">Has it got subtle grain?  I can''t seem to pick anything up - perhaps my screen?</td>', 'Has it got subtle grain?  I can''t seem to pick anything up - perhaps my screen?', '2005-10-24 21:30:47.000000', NULL, 1),
