(1847617, 247888, 29474, '<td valign="top">When I originally saw this I got the idea that it was a daughter encouraging her father. So that is how I will keep thinking of it, even though I know it is not so.</td>', 'When I originally saw this I got the idea that it was a daughter encouraging her father. So that is how I will keep thinking of it, even though I know it is not so.', '2005-11-08 14:37:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(1850968, 246927, 30817, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by woutje:</b></div><hr/><i> For me, this image has been grained to the point that it has become a digital art image rather than a photo. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>....and we certainly would not want that; now, would we?  Sheesh! It seems like someone using a camera for anything rather than literal representation is thought to be a witch on this site.  This is a terrific example of creative photography on a thinking level, Eleanor.  Your fresh insights and the growth I have seen you display over the past year, have been very rewarding.  I know you won''t be dissuaded as a result of not conforming to the "rules" on this site. (One of which is that in order for the shot to be successful, there should be something liquid caught splashing upward in the frame.)</td>', 'Originally posted by woutje: For me, this image has been grained to the point that it has become a digital art image rather than a photo.  ....and we certainly would not want that; now, would we?  Sheesh! It seems like someone using a camera for anything rather than literal representation is thought to be a witch on this site.  This is a terrific example of creative photography on a thinking level, Eleanor.  Your fresh insights and the growth I have seen you display over the past year, have been very rewarding.  I know you won''t be dissuaded as a result of not conforming to the "rules" on this site. (One of which is that in order for the shot to be successful, there should be something liquid caught splashing upward in the frame.)', '2005-11-09 12:53:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(1852448, 247358, 34013, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Alienyst:</b></div><hr/><i> The challenge was to show image grain in your picture - not part of your picture. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>in response:  maybe you should go back and read the challenge description before you go around judging and leaving unapplicable feedback. the challenge description says:<br/> Create an image where image grain or "noise" is an integral part of the message of your photo.<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by Alienyst: The challenge was to show image grain in your picture - not part of your picture.   in response:  maybe you should go back and read the challenge description before you go around judging and leaving unapplicable feedback. the challenge description says: Create an image where image grain or "noise" is an integral part of the message of your photo.', '2005-11-09 19:19:04.000000', NULL, 0),
